# Master Context

At the start of every session, read `AGENTS.md` in the root of this repository.
Then read any `AGENTS/` files relevant to the current task.

Do not proceed with any task until you have confirmed:
1. The 4-layer architecture and what imports what (AGENTS/00-architecture.md)
2. Where the relevant service/component for this task lives (AGENTS.md section 6)
3. Which existing patterns to replicate (AGENTS/03-angular-conventions.md)
4. The definition of done (AGENTS.md section 7)

If AGENTS.md does not exist, stop and tell the developer to run:
`git pull` — the file should be present on the main branch.

## JIRA Integration

If the developer provides a JIRA ticket ID (e.g. "implement NCO-1234"), use the
Atlassian MCP to fetch the story before doing anything else:
- Read the Acceptance Criteria as the technical requirements
- Use them to expand the intent just as the Requirement Agent would from free text
- Reference the ticket ID in the commit message and PR title
